Here is the commit message:
OOZIE-2102. Streaming actions are broken cause of incorrect
 method signature. Contributed by Harsh J.

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by an incorrect method signature in the `StreamingMain` class, which used a `Configuration` object instead of the more specific `JobConf` object. This led to improper handling of job configurations necessary for streaming actions, resulting in failures when executing those actions. The removal of the `addActionConf` method call further indicates that the previous configuration handling was not correctly propagating the necessary settings for streaming jobs.

Here is the patch:

